2026-08-22T14:19:44.9890766Z [36;1m# Compile on every core the runner has, not the two this used to pin.[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9891579Z [36;1m# Standard GitHub-hosted Linux runners have been 4-vCPU since 2024, so[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9892058Z [36;1m# -j2 left half the box idle through the phase that dominates a build:[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9892494Z [36;1m# measured on a 4-core box, 8 vendored unity objects with ccache[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9892917Z [36;1m# disabled take 70.8 s at -j2 and 43.1 s at -j4 -- 1.64x, at identical[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9893354Z [36;1m# user time. Peak RSS per unity object is ~834 MB, so four in flight is[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9893751Z [36;1m# ~3.3 GB of the runner's 16 GB.[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9894106Z [36;1m# detectCores() can return NA on exotic platforms; fall back to the old[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9894611Z [36;1m# value there. `--as-cran` sets _R_CHECK_LIMIT_CORES_, but that polices[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9895076Z [36;1m# the *package's* runtime parallelism, not compilation, so this is safe.[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9896024Z [36;1mncores="$(Rscript --vanilla -e 'n <- parallel::detectCores(); cat(if (is.na(n) || n < 1) 2L else as.integer(n))')"[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9896582Z [36;1mecho "MAKEFLAGS = -j${ncores}" >> ~/.R/Makevars[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9896903Z [36;1mecho "===== generated ~/.R/Makevars ====="[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9897172Z [36;1mcat ~/.R/Makevars[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9897569Z [36;1mecho "==================================="[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9897815Z [36;1m[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9898079Z [36;1mecho 'CCACHE_SLOPPINESS=locale,time_macros' | tee -a $GITHUB_ENV[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9898412Z [36;1m[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9898681Z [36;1m# Do NOT export UserNM here, however tempting the `UserNM=true` trick[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9899131Z [36;1m# from AGENTS.md looks. It is a development shortcut, not a CI setting.[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9899471Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9899671Z [36;1m# R takes the nm program from $UserNM in[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9900038Z [36;1m# tools:::read_symbols_from_object_file, and that function serves two[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9900477Z [36;1m# callers, not one: building `symbols.rds` at install time (which[0m
2026-08-22T14:19:44.9900852Z [36;1m# src/Makevars puts on the `all:` target), *and*[0m
